# What the study of the old body's natural-language lane found (study/r2/gap-natural-language-lane.md, closing gap G3 of the first-round critique). The study ran no program: every verdict number below is a number recorded in a file.

n: 3.10
name: natural-language-lane
kind: hub
is: The old body's natural-language translator is 70 lines: two languages (English, Indonesian), one sentence construction, two one-word slots, 52 lexicon rows, ASCII only. The pivot is a content-interned node: its category is a numeric coordinate, its two children are strings holding arrival-order labels. The test of the north star's example was deleted on 2026-09-29; one band over five invented words stands. Seven neutral-id schemes exist, none joined to the translator. A 10,000-row label table is 57.0% machine translation, 0 rows reviewed.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1
name: translator
kind: hub
is: nl-translate.fk holds two grammars as data, a 52-row lexicon with first-match lookup, a pivot node of category 1.2.99.33 over two label strings, and one hand-written decoder per language. Text handling is ASCII only. A lexicon miss passes the surface word into the pivot and a parse failure is the string PARSE-FAIL; neither is a fault. The fragment is one copular construction, two languages, 50 words per language, and the node's identity sits on the spelling of its labels.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.1
name: grammar-and-decoder
kind: observation
is: In nl-translate.fk each of the two languages has a grammar value of two rules; the content rule is a fixed token sequence (the X is Y; X adalah Y) with two one-word capture slots and emits one node kind, property. Output text is built by one hand-written concatenation function per language, which does not read the grammar.
status: observed
src: 2.18.2#22-23 2.18.2#61-62 2.18.2#67-68 2.18.7#1109-1131
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.2
name: lexicon-rows
kind: observation
is: The translator's lexicon is 52 rows of (symbol, phase, English, Indonesian): 7 seed rows n0..n6, 40 corpus rows c0..c39 and 5 minted rows m1257..m1261, giving 50 distinct words per language. Lookup scans for the first row whose column equals the word, so home (rows c16, c21, c23) always answers c16. Seven rows are spelled the same in both columns.
status: observed
src: 2.18.2#35 2.18.2#41-46 2.18.3#15-17 2.18.1#4
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.3
name: pivot-node
kind: observation
is: The translator's pivot is intern_node(bp("property"), [string, string]): a composite whose category is the coordinate 1.2.99.33 and whose two children are string leaves holding lexicon symbols (n0). Six natural-language blueprints are reserved at 1.2.99.32 to 37 (fact, property, isa, relation, question, meaning); only property is used at head.
status: observed
src: 2.18.2#58-59 2.18.9#943 2.18.8#93-108 2.1.10#37
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.4
name: ascii-floor
kind: observation
is: The translator's text handling is ASCII only: str-normalize lowercases A to Z through a 26-letter map and drops six punctuation marks, and both grammars capture slots with the class alpha, which is ASCII letters and underscore. A class letter that also accepts any byte of 128 or more is defined in bmf-core.fk; no grammar at head uses that class.
status: observed
src: 2.18.10#12-28 2.18.8#330-333 2.18.8#352-359 2.18.2#22-23
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.5
name: failure-arms
kind: observation
is: On a lexicon miss the translator's lookup returns the surface word unchanged, and that word becomes a child of the pivot. On a parse failure g-parse returns the string leaf PARSE-FAIL as a value. The translator calls g-parse, the prefix matcher, and not g-parse-full, the whole-source parser. None of the three cases raises a fault.
status: observed
src: 2.18.2#43-45 2.18.2#58 2.18.2#67-68 2.18.7#3-5 2.18.7#1094-1107
limit: The study ran no sentence through the translator: what tr-en-id answers for a sentence outside the template, or for one with trailing words, was not observed.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.6
name: corpus-rows-and-coverage
kind: observation
is: The translator's 40 corpus rows are single-word ASCII strings found at the same key in two interface message files, en.json and id.json, which exist only in the parent repository; the runner that would regenerate the rows is recorded as not built. The homecoming corpus holds 1,070 rows (ids 601 to 1683); 5 of their words have a lexicon row.
status: observed
src: 2.18.4#18-19 2.18.4#33-56 2.3#web/messages 2.18.11 2.18.3#15-17 2.18.5#7-14 2.18.1#4
limit: The 5-of-1,070 figure (0.47%) is the study's static join of two files, not a run of the coverage lens.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.7
name: label-is-the-identity
kind: finding
is: Sentences in two languages intern to one pivot node exactly when both lexicon directions return the same symbol string for each slot. The symbols n<i>, c<i> and m<id> are arrival-order labels and are the node's content, so renaming a symbol changes the node; the comment at nl-translate.fk lines 24-28 says identity is invariant under renaming.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.10.1.2 3.10.1.3 3.10.1.5
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.1.8
name: fragment
kind: finding
is: The old translator covers one construction: copular predication with a one-word subject and a one-word predicate, in English and Indonesian, over 50 words per language. The translator handles no verb other than the copula, plural, tense, negation, question, modifier, multi-word slot, agreement, reordering or choice between senses by context.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.10.1.1 3.10.1.2
src: 2.18.33#9-13 2.18.33#110-135 2.18.28#317-323 2.18.21#4
limit: The claim covers the translator only. Elsewhere at head a sample grammar parses "negate 12" and "twice 5 plus 3" into arithmetic recipes, the dictionary of meaning recipes selects among a word's mappings by context, and the phrase lenses hold an enquiry as a fixed phrase; none of the three imports the translator.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

n: 3.10.2
name: witness
kind: hub
is: The north star says two example sentences intern to one node. The test of that pair was deleted on 2026-09-29 by the commit that last edited the north-star line. At head one band of sixteen bits calls the translator, on five invented words; its recorded verdict 65535 is dated 2026-09-28 and was not re-run. Thirteen further languages and nearly every band of the lane left in the same cut. The claim that a numeric space is the root of natural languages rests on one sentence shape, two languages and a hand-made table.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-natural-language-lane

